<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Southbrook Kitchen 3D Configurator — Canonical catalog DIMENSION overlay.
  Split 2026-07-01 (E2E audit §4.A) — sibling to canonical_catalog_tag.xml.

  This file carries the per-template dimension seed values
  (southbrook_width_in, southbrook_height_in, southbrook_depth_in)
  for the 11 canonical templates. Loaded with `noupdate="1"` so a
  customer or rep who edits a template's dimensions from the UI
  does NOT get their edit clobbered on the next module -u.

  Before this split (2026-07-01 audit §4.A), dimensions lived
  inside canonical_catalog_tag.xml with noupdate="0", so every -u
  reverted UI edits back to these seed values.

  Follow-up P1 (documented in the header of the pre-split file):
  compute variant-level southbrook_width_in from
  product_template_attribute_value_ids so each variant reports its
  true width and the template-level scalar becomes advisory.

  Dimension source:
    * southbrook_width_in — MIDPOINT of each template's width envelope
      per Southbrook_Excel_to_Odoo_Mapping §3.1. Width is a VARIANT
      attribute on the canonicals (attr_width value_ids), so this
      template-level scalar is a fallback the configurator uses when
      no variant is picked.
    * southbrook_height_in / southbrook_depth_in — NA-cabinetry
      standards. If Southbrook's Consolidated Dataset differs,
      override these values here.
-->
<odoo noupdate="1">

